ok system."},"1121":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-146","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#custom-reward-types","content":"For custom reward types, the `name` field is just a **unique identifier** used for internal tracking and logging - it doesn't need to be an actual item in your inventory. Since custom rewards aren't real items, you must also provide `label` and `image` explicitly."},"1122":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-147","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#custom-reward-types","content":"Custom reward types require a registered reward hook to handle them. If no hook is registered, the system will fall back to default item behavior and log a warning."},"1123":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-148","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#how-custom-rewards-work","content":"When a player wins an item with a custom `rewardType`, the system looks for a registered hook for that type"},"1124":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-149","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#how-custom-rewards-work","content":"If a hook exists and returns `true`, the hook handled the reward"},"1125":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-150","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#how-custom-rewards-work","content":"If a hook returns `false`/`nil`, the system falls back to default item behavior"},"1126":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-151","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#how-custom-rewards-work","content":"If no hook exists, a warning is logged and the system falls back to default item behavior"},"1127":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-152","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#how-custom-rewards-work","content":"This ensures rewards are never silently lost - if something isn't configured correctly, players still receive items."},"1128":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-153","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#registering-reward-hooks","content":"Register hooks from your own resource to handle custom reward types:"},"1129":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-154","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#registering-reward-hooks","content":"See the Server Exports page for full API documentation."},"1130":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-155","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#complete-vehicle-crate-example","content":"Here's a complete example of a lootbox that awards vehicles using custom reward types:"},"1131":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-156","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#understanding-weight-distribution","content":"The weight system is flexible and doesn't require weights to sum to 100. The probability of each item is calculated as:"},"1132":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-157","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#example-calculation","content":"If you have items with weights: 80, 15, 4, 1 (total: 100)"},"1133":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-158","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#example-calculation","content":"Item with weight 80: 80/100 = 80% chance"},"1134":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-159","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#example-calculation","content":"Item with weight 15: 15/100 = 15% chance"},"1135":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-160","pa